;
; demand_neighborhood_nested_witness -- the FLAGS-TWIN of
; demand_neighborhood_mono_witness (s37 S2a, panel-mandated): the SAME program
; text compiled under `-demand -demand-instance` (.drflags), so its four-mode
; stdout runs the NESTED keyed-instance lowering. Its stdout golden is a
; SYMLINK to goldens/demand_neighborhood_mono_witness.stdout (the
; key_tc_witness twin mechanism; bless_copy refuses to write through it), so
; nested==flat answer identity is enforced BY THE SUITE on this case, while
; the mono twin's own .eqgate re-proves it live from the flat side.
;
; Its OWN rel.opt golden is the byte pin of the nested `-rel-out` surface --
; the DRInstance descriptor render + kSubgraphInstantiate=1/kInstanceSeal=1
; census + the excised guard-join web (no kEagerJoin/kJoinEmit) -- the ONE
; goldened view of the nested Rel-IR until the RP-6 @key twins return
; (S2c). The program text MUST stay byte-identical to the mono twin's; only
; the header comment differs.

#message add_edge(u64 From, u64 To).

#local edge(u64 From, u64 To).
edge(From, To) : add_edge(From, To).

#query neighborhood(bound u64 Start, free u64 Node) : edge(Start, Node).
